  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">RTK + Vision vs. Buried Boundary Wire</h3>

  <p>If you've researched robot mowers before, you've likely seen boundary-wire systems, the older, still-common approach where a physical wire is buried or pinned around the perimeter of the area to be mowed, and the robot detects that wire to know where to stop. It works, but it comes with real tradeoffs Yarbo's approach was built to avoid.</p>

