  <p>For a one-acre property paying a lawn service roughly $60 a visit through a 20-week season, that's about $1,200 a year before snow or leaf cleanup are even part of the conversation. At today's price of {{ yp_lmp_bundle.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}, a Yarbo Lawn Mower Pro bundle works out to roughly {{ yp_lmp_bundle.price | divided_by: 120000 }} to {{ yp_lmp_bundle.price | divided_by: 120000 | plus: 1 }} years of that single expense, and every additional module you add afterward extends the same base investment into the next season instead of starting the calculation over from zero. Add the Snow Blower Module and you're also no longer paying a plow service per-storm, and add the Leaf Blower Module and the fall cleanup crew invoice disappears too. The math compounds in the Core's favor the more seasons you put it to work.</p>

