  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Maintenance and Longevity</h3>

  <p>The Core itself has few consumable parts, most of the wear happens on the module: mower blades, snow blower chute components, and similar wear items are the things you'll periodically replace, the same as with any equivalent traditional machine. What you're not doing is separate engine maintenance, oil changes, or winterizing three different small engines every year, since the Core is electric and the modules attach to a single drive and battery system. Every Core and module carries Yarbo's 2-year limited warranty, and Yard Automation Pros helps you file and follow up on any claim.</p>

  <hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;margin:48px 0 0;">
  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:48px;">Common Questions About the Yarbo System</h3>

  <p><strong>Do I need to buy a new Core for every module?</strong><br>
  No. One Core runs every module Yarbo makes. You buy the Core once and add modules over time as your seasonal needs expand, rather than buying three complete machines.</p>

  <p><strong>How long does it take to swap modules?</strong><br>
  A few minutes. It's designed for a homeowner to do it directly, not a scheduled technician visit, so switching from the mower to the snow blower as winter approaches isn't a project.</p>

  <p><strong>Does it work without a buried boundary wire?</strong><br>
  Yes. RTK + Vision navigation maps your property from your phone. No trenching, no wire, no beacons, and no wire to dig up if you change your landscaping later.</p>

  <p><strong>What slope can it actually handle?</strong><br>
  The tracked Core is rated for slopes up to 70% grade (35 degrees) with the mower and blower modules. With the Snow Blower Module, Yarbo rates it for 36% (20 degrees).</p>

  <p><strong>Will it work under tree cover, where GPS is usually weaker?</strong><br>
  Yes, this is specifically where RTK + Vision outperforms GPS-only systems. The binocular vision and inertial sensors keep the Core tracking its position accurately even when satellite signal weakens briefly under a dense canopy.</p>

  <p><strong>What's the warranty?</strong><br>
  Every Core and module carries Yarbo's 2-year limited warranty.</p>

  <p><strong>Can I finance a Core and module together?</strong><br>
  Yes, financing is available at checkout through Shop Pay Installments across the full system, Core and module together or added later.</p>

  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Ownership, Handled</h3>

  <p>Every Yarbo Core and module ships free, arriving approximately 10 to 14 days after payment. Financing is available at checkout through Shop Pay Installments, so the cost spreads over time rather than landing as one lump sum. And you're not buying this from a manufacturer's storefront with no one to call, Yard Automation Pros provides real, US-based expert guidance before and after your purchase, from picking the right modules for your property to helping you get the most out of the system once it's running. If something isn't working the way it should, you have a real person to reach, not a support ticket queue.</p>

